  "term": "uncinate fasciculus",
  "definition": "The uncinate fasciculus is a hook-shaped bundle of white matter fibers that links parts of the temporal lobe, including the uncus and temporal pole, with the limbic system and frontal lobe. It also connects with the amygdala proper.",
